steps.explanation:
Short $L$ and open $C$: the current through $R_1$ and $R_2$ is $i_L = \frac{V_s}{R_1+R_2}$ = {{Vs/(R1+R2)|A}}. The shorted $L$ ties the right end of $R_2$ to the bottom wire, so $v_C = v_a = i_LR_2$ = {{Vs*R2/(R1+R2)|V}}.
$w_C$ = 0.5 × {{C|F}} × ({{Vs*R2/(R1+R2)|V}})² = {{0.5*C*(Vs*R2/(R1+R2))^2|J}}
$w_L$ = 0.5 × {{L|H}} × ({{Vs/(R1+R2)|A}})² = {{0.5*L*(Vs/(R1+R2))^2|J}}
Total: {{0.5*C*(Vs*R2/(R1+R2))^2 + 0.5*L*(Vs/(R1+R2))^2|J}}.
